-- S23 Maharashtra prose — ranjangaon
-- Verdict matrix: 8 go / 1 skip / 3 wait
-- Anchors: Mahaganpati — 4th Ashtavinayak in yatra order, only ONE of 8 Maha Ganapati murtis in India (10-trunked 20-armed form), 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa elevation, Shivaji-era underground sealed original shrine, LION vahana (not mooshik), winter-solstice sun-ray temple orientation Dec-Jan touches idol, Pune 50km via NH753 Pune-Ahmednagar Highway

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('ranjangaon', 1, 'go', 5, 'January at Ranjangaon is among the year-best months — and uniquely so. The Mahaganpati temple, the fourth in the traditional Ashtavinayak yatra and the only one of the eight that houses a Maha Ganapati murti (the 10-trunked, 20-armed form, of which only eight examples exist in all India), runs continuous puja at the freshest weather and at its astronomically unique winter-solstice phenomenon. The temple east-facing orientation is calibrated such that through Dec-Jan dawn sunlight passes through the main entrance and strikes directly on the central murti face — a sun-ray darshan window of 8-12 minutes each morning. Pre-dawn pilgrim flow builds for the 6:45-7am sun-ray slot. The vahana is the LION (not the standard mooshik mouse) — unusual among Ganesha temples. The original underground Shivaji-era shrine sits sealed below; the visible structure is the 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa elevation. Daytime 15-29C. Pune drive 50km/75 min via NH753. Sankashti Chaturthi early month brings standard Tuesday density.', 'January is the year-best Ranjangaon month — winter-solstice sun-ray darshan touches the 10-trunked 20-armed Maha Ganapati murti at 6:45-7am daily. LION vahana (unusual). 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure. 15-29C. Pune 50km/75 min.', NULL),
('ranjangaon', 2, 'go', 5, 'February at Ranjangaon makes Maghi Ganesh Jayanti — Magh Shukla Chaturthi Wednesday 4 February 2026 — a peak event. The Mahaganpati murti (the 10-trunked, 20-armed Maha Ganapati form unique among the eight Ashtavinayak temples) receives the pre-dawn maha-abhishek ritual; palki processions run morning and evening. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 3 February 2026 compounding pilgrim density. The winter-solstice sun-ray darshan window — where dawn light through the east-facing entrance strikes the central murti face — continues through the first week. Daytime 17-31C. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure (with the sealed Shivaji-era underground original below the visible sanctum) and the LION vahana iconography draw heritage-pilgrim flow beyond the festival pilgrims. The 50km Pune drive via NH753 takes 90 minutes on festival days. Lodgings book 2 weeks ahead at ₹800-2,200 festival rates. Devotees attempting both Theur and Ranjangaon in a single day from Pune time this window.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4 + Angarki Feb 3 — Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti maha-abhishek. Sun-ray darshan continues first week. 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure, LION vahana. Lodgings ₹800-2,200.', NULL),
('ranjangaon', 3, 'go', 4, 'March at Ranjangaon holds clean operational temperature through first three weeks. Gudi Padwa Thursday 19 March 2026 brings extended morning ritual at Mahaganpati and Marathi New Year pilgrim flow from Pune (Ranjangaon sits 50km out on the Pune-Ahmednagar highway and connects easily with Ahmednagar-region devotees as well). Daytime 21-34C, nights 15-17C. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti runs standard 5am-9pm darshan; the LION vahana iconography clearly visible against the cool stone interior. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure and the sealed Shivaji-era underground original at full ritual tempo. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard Tuesday density. The 50km NH753 drive remains 75 minutes. By final week the heat ramp arrives — mid-day temple courtyard becomes uncomfortable. Lodgings ₹600-1,500. Last clean-comfort window before April compression. Combine with Shivneri Fort 30km north for a heritage day-trip extension.', 'Gudi Padwa Mar 19 extended morning ritual. 21-34C through first 3 weeks. 10-trunked 20-armed Mahaganpati at full schedule. NH753 50km/75 min. Combine with Shivneri Fort 30km north. Last clean window before April.', NULL),
('ranjangaon', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April pushes Ranjangaon into heat-compromise territory. Daytime 26-39C on the Pune plateau; the temple courtyard stone holds heat 8am-7pm. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti darshan compresses to pre-9am and post-5pm windows. The cool stone interior of the 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa-era sanctum holds 33-35C — slightly cooler than the open pradakshina but still warm. The LION vahana sculpture sits in the open courtyard at full afternoon heat exposure. Pilgrim arrivals thin sharply through month; lodging rates drop to ₹500-1,200. The 50km NH753 drive in an AC bus remains tolerable — Ranjangaon sits less remotely than Lenyadri or Siddhatek and pulls dedicated dawn-slot pilgrim flow even in April heat. The sealed Shivaji-era underground original below the visible sanctum holds cooler temperatures (28-30C) but is closed to public access. The full sun-ray darshan window has closed (it runs Dec-Jan). Push to October.', 'April compresses Mahaganpati darshan to dawn and dusk windows. 26-39C. Open pradakshina + LION vahana courtyard uncomfortable past 10am. NH753 drive easy. Sun-ray window closed. Push to October.', 'April runs at fragmented schedule. 26-39C heat compresses the 10-trunked 20-armed murti darshan to dawn fragments. The LION vahana courtyard sculpture at full afternoon heat. Full temple experience does not happen.'),
('ranjangaon', 5, 'skip', 2, 'May is unviable Ranjangaon. Daytime 30-42C on the Pune plateau; the temple stone courtyard hits 50C surface noon. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti darshan continues but the practical pilgrim experience collapses — even the 5am dawn slot opens at 28C and reaches 35C by closing. The cool stone interior of the 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa-era sanctum holds 33-35C through day. The LION vahana sculpture in the open courtyard at year-peak heat exposure. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 5 May 2026 — dedicated pilgrim flow continues at modest density but most yatra-pilgrims skip Ranjangaon through May. Lodgings drop to ₹500-1,000 deep off-season. The 50km Pune-Ahmednagar Highway drive remains drivable but the temple visit itself is the failure point. The sun-ray darshan window has long closed; the temple sits in its low-event slot. Push to October.', NULL, 'May 30-42C — temple courtyard 50C surface noon. Even 5am dawn slot opens at 28C, reaches 35C by closing. LION vahana courtyard at year-peak heat exposure. Sun-ray darshan window closed. Full temple experience collapses to fragmented dawn slot. Push to October.'),
('ranjangaon', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks southwest monsoon arrival in Ranjangaon. First-week rains break the heat — daytime 22-32C, nights 19-21C. The 50km NH753 Pune-Ahmednagar drive remains workable but adds 15-20 minutes through monsoon-section caution. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti runs standard 5am-9pm darshan; the 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure and the LION vahana courtyard sit in fresh post-rain Pune-plateau context — the green setting around the temple is among the better viewing conditions of the year. The sealed Shivaji-era underground original below holds dry through monsoon (the temple sits on elevated ground above natural drainage). Sankashti Chaturthi late month brings modest pilgrim flow. Pilgrim lodging ₹600-1,400 with monsoon discount. Time the visit to morning windows after the previous night rain has cleared.', 'June monsoon arrival — 22-32C, fresh post-rain green around Ranjangaon. 10-trunked 20-armed Mahaganpati + LION vahana courtyard at clean visual context. NH753 50km drive +15-20 min monsoon caution.', 'June transition month — fresh green visual context but operational drag. NH753 50km drive 90-95 min, expect at least one wet darshan stretch. Mahaganpati morning-only reliable on heavy-rain days.'),
('ranjangaon', 7, 'wait', 3, 'July holds monsoon-peak rainfall on the Pune plateau — Ranjangaon receives 350-500mm. The temple complex sits on elevated ground and remains dry; the 50km NH753 Pune-Ahmednagar drive takes 90-100 minutes through caution sections. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti runs morning-only schedule reliably on monsoon days. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure and the LION vahana sculpture sit against a monsoon-green setting that is photographically striking. The sealed Shivaji-era underground original holds dry through monsoon. AC-bus packages drop to ₹350-600 day-trip rates. Sankashti Chaturthi pilgrim flow modest. Lodgings ₹500-1,200 at deep monsoon rates. Time the visit to morning windows after overnight rain has cleared; combine with Shivneri Fort 30km north only on confirmed-dry-day windows.', 'July monsoon-soaked Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti visually striking, 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure + LION vahana in monsoon-green setting. NH753 50km drive 90-100 min. AC-bus ₹350-600. Morning-only reliable.', 'July monsoon peak — NH753 drive 90-100 min through caution sections. AC-bus services on weather-watch suspension on heavy-rain days. The reliable yatra experience does not happen at standard tempo.'),
('ranjangaon', 8, 'go', 4, 'August at Ranjangaon opens with Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday 4 August 2026 — drawing committed Pune and Ahmednagar pilgrim flow despite the rain. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti runs extended ritual schedule for the festival. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure and the LION vahana courtyard at full ritual tempo. Daytime 22-31C, humid; rainfall sustained at 300-400mm through month. The 50km NH753 drive takes 80-90 minutes through caution sections. Pilgrim density picks up through final week as the Ganesh Chaturthi build approaches. The Ahmednagar pilgrim flow (Ranjangaon sits on the Pune-Ahmednagar highway and attracts the Ahmednagar Marathi heritage community alongside the Pune devotees) builds notably in August. Lodgings rise to ₹600-1,500 from early-month discount. Combine with Shivneri Fort 30km north on confirmed-dry-day windows.', 'Angarki Chaturthi Tue Aug 4 — Mahaganpati extended ritual. 10-trunked 20-armed murti + LION vahana + 1790 Peshwa structure. NH753 50km drive 80-90 min. Pre-Ganesh-Chaturthi build through final week. Ahmednagar pilgrim flow builds.', NULL),
('ranjangaon', 9, 'go', 5, 'September makes Ranjangaon a Ganesh Chaturthi anchor. The festival (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi) falls Saturday 12 September 2026 — the 10-day festival running through Anant Chaturdashi Tuesday 22 September 2026. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti — the only one of its kind among the eight Ashtavinayak — receives continuous palki processions, special pre-dawn maha-abhishek every morning, full puran-poli and ukadiche-modak prasad distribution. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure runs at festival saturation. The LION vahana courtyard hosts the main festival palki staging. Daytime 22-30C with monsoon tail rains tapering through first week. The 50km NH753 drive takes 2-2.5 hours through festival traffic; private operators run 3-day Ashtavinayak packages with Ranjangaon Day 1-2. Lodgings book 90 days ahead at ₹1,500-3,500 festival rates. The Mahaganpati specialness — the unique 10-trunked 20-armed murti form — draws dedicated pilgrim density beyond the standard yatra.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12-22 — the only Maha Ganapati (10-trunked 20-armed) murti among 8 Ashtavinayak at festival saturation. Continuous palki processions, pre-dawn maha-abhishek, LION vahana courtyard staging. Lodgings ₹1,500-3,500.', NULL),
('ranjangaon', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is post-monsoon ideal Ranjangaon. The 10-day Ganesh Chaturthi peak has dispersed; through first two weeks the residue continues at strong tempo, then settles into clean operational tempo. Daytime 19-32C, nights 16-18C. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti runs at full schedule against a green Pune-plateau backdrop. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure (with the sealed Shivaji-era underground original below) and the LION vahana courtyard at clean visual presentation. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 6 October 2026 bringing dedicated pilgrim density without the September overload. The 50km NH753 drive returns to 75-minute standard time. Lodgings drop to ₹700-1,800. The pre-winter window before the winter-solstice sun-ray darshan opens in December — visit Ranjangaon now if the sun-ray phenomenon is not on the itinerary. Combine with Shivneri Fort 30km north.', 'Post-monsoon ideal — 19-32C, green Pune-plateau backdrop. 10-trunked 20-armed Mahaganpati at clean visual presentation. Angarki Tue Oct 6. NH753 75 min. Pre-winter window before Dec-Jan sun-ray opens. Combine with Shivneri Fort.', NULL),
('ranjangaon', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is the year-best Ranjangaon stretch. The post-monsoon Pune-plateau green holds through first two weeks; daytime 16-30C, nights 12-14C — the sharpest cool weather of the year. The Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti darshan at full 5am-9pm schedule with light woolens needed for the 5am slot. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure (with the sealed Shivaji-era original below the visible sanctum) and the LION vahana courtyard at cleanest visual presentation. The winter-solstice sun-ray darshan phenomenon — where dawn light through the east-facing entrance strikes the central murti — starts its build-up through late November. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard density. The 50km NH753 drive runs cleanest of the year — 70-75 minutes on weekday mornings. Pilgrim lodgings ₹700-1,800. Combine with Shivneri Fort 30km north for a Maharashtra-heritage day-trip extension.', 'November year-best — 16-30C, sharpest cool of year. 10-trunked 20-armed Mahaganpati + LION vahana courtyard at cleanest visual. Winter-solstice sun-ray darshan build-up late month. NH753 70-75 min. Combine with Shivneri Fort 30km.', NULL),
('ranjangaon', 12, 'go', 5, 'December at Ranjangaon is another year-best stretch. The winter-solstice sun-ray darshan phenomenon — where dawn light through the east-facing entrance strikes the central Mahaganpati 10-trunked 20-armed murti face for 8-12 minutes each morning — runs at peak alignment through Dec 5-25. Pre-dawn pilgrim flow builds for the 6:45-7am sun-ray slot; book accommodation the night before to make the dawn timing. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 1 December 2026 — the auspicious month-opener combined with the sun-ray phenomenon makes Dec 1 the heaviest single-day density of December. Daytime 14-29C, nights 9-11C — year-coolest stretch; light woolens essential for the 5am pre-darshan wait. The 1790 Madhavrao II Peshwa structure and the LION vahana courtyard at peak visual presentation. The 50km NH753 drive runs heavy weekend traffic through Pune-tourist-escape season. Lodgings rise to ₹800-2,000.', 'Dec 1 Angarki Chaturthi + winter-solstice sun-ray darshan peak (Dec 5-25, 6:45-7am, 8-12 min). 14-29C year-coolest. 10-trunked 20-armed Mahaganpati at sun-ray illumination. Lodgings ₹800-2,000. Book night before for 5am slot.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
  score = EXCLUDED.score,
  prose_lead = EXCLUDED.prose_lead,
  why_go = EXCLUDED.why_go,
  why_not = EXCLUDED.why_not;
